{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786481692,"nonce":"FFEEJV0wi7Tdu+rurkVdHYLK140=","title":"**What is wrong.** `web/src/features/settings/tuningCopy.ts` defines **9 `guide()` closures** — one each for `refire_grace_s` (`:370`), `group_close_delay_s` (`:421`), `resolve_grace_s` (`:461`), `flap_threshold` (`:493`), `flap_window_s` (`:538`), `flap_digest_interval_s` (`:585`), `storm_window_s` (`:648`), `storm_cooldown_s` (`:689`) and `unacked_reminder_after_s` (`:726`). Each one does arithmetic over the operator's own Alertmanager timings and returns a verdict plus, at **14 sites**, a `suggest` number. That number is not advice the operator reads and weighs: `TuningSection.tsx:1614-1626` renders it as a `use {N}` button whose `onClick` writes it straight into the field. **There is no `tuningCopy.test.ts` and no `TuningSection.test.tsx`.** Zero of the nine are tested.","message":"**The demonstration.** `tuningCopy.ts:370-400` decides \"Unreachable\" for `refire_grace_s` from `ASSUMED_RULE_FOR_S + group_interval`, compares that against `group_interval * 2`, and offers `Math.max(ruleFloor, gi * 2)` as the value to write. The comment immediately above it (`:366-369`) records that an **earlier version of this arithmetic was wrong in production** — it \"reported the old 600s default as comfortably fine while the modal `for: 15m` rule could never reach it.\" A closure with that history and no test is the whole finding. The only coverage over this screen is `settings-contract.test.tsx`, **5 tests**, every one of them about bounds and enum membership; the word `guide` does not appear in any test file in `web/src`.\n\nADR 0021 does exempt this screen, and the exemption is precisely what makes it a defect. `docs/adr/0021-correctness-and-testing-strategy.md:101-102`: *\"**The SolidJS UI is exempt** and stays grow-from-bugs, covered by the Playwright suite in `web/e2e/`. A settings *form* is UI; the setting *behind* it is not, and falls under the config-knob rule above.\"* A closure that computes a `group_interval`-derived floor and writes it into `refire_grace_s` is the setting behind the form, not the form. And the exemption's designated safety net does not exist: `web/e2e/` contains only `.gitkeep`, and `web/package.json` has no Playwright dependency and no e2e script.\n\n**Why it matters.** These functions tell a 3am operator which number to type, and a wrong verdict is indistinguishable from a right one — it arrives in the same `Note`, with the same one-click button, in the same confident prose. The failure is silent and lands in a config knob that governs whether a re-fire opens a new Slack thread.\n\n**Where.** The obstacle to testing is that the arithmetic is welded to a 2915-line pair. `TuningSection.tsx` is 1876 lines and `tuningCopy.ts` is 1039, and each holds two unrelated subsystems whose seam is already drawn as a comment divider rather than a file boundary. The read-only Alertmanager route-provenance viewer is contiguous and touches no form state: `TuningSection.tsx:116-193` (`amRefOf`, `reachingRoutes`, `routeLabel`, `usesDeprecatedMatchers`, `knownCount`) plus `:699-1171` (`ProvenanceBadge` through `SourceTimings`/`AlertmanagerPanel`) — **551 lines** — and `tuningCopy.ts:54-248`, **195 lines**. Its only bridge to the knob form is `Ctl.am` at `TuningSection.tsx:216`. The knob half has its own named seam already: `KNOB_GROUPS` at `tuningCopy.ts:881`, 5 groups over 17 knobs.\n\n**Scope.** large\n\n**Done when.** The 9 `guide()` closures live in a module with a test per closure — each asserting the level and the `suggest` value against fixed Alertmanager numbers, including the `null` return when provenance is `unknown` — the Alertmanager viewer is extracted to `tuning/alertmanagerRef.ts` and `tuning/AlertmanagerOrigin.tsx`, and `TuningSection.tsx` is under ~600 lines.","files":null}]}